<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Blaauwberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1806">1806</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Blouberg · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Blaauwberg was fought on 8 January 1806 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-town">Cape Town</a>, when a British force under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-baird">David Baird</a> defeated the Batavian garrison of Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-willem-janssens">Jan Willem Janssens</a>. The Cape surrendered days later, beginning permanent British rule over the colony, which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> formally ceded in 1814. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> wanted the Cape to protect the sea route to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-blaauwberg.jpg" alt="Battle of Blaauwberg" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Undated-painting-showing-the-1806-Battle-of-Blaauwberg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Peace of Amiens returned the Cape to the Batavian Republic in 1803, but a British force under General David Baird landed again and won the <b>Battle of Blaauwberg</b> on 8 January 1806, and the Netherlands formally ceded the colony in the Anglo-Dutch convention of 1814.</blockquote><a href="/empire/cape-colony">Cape Colony · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Britain seized the Cape in 1795 after the Battle of Muizenberg, returned it to the Batavian Republic in 1803 and took it again after the <b>Battle of Blaauwberg</b> in 1806.</blockquote><a href="/state/dutch-cape-colony">Dutch Cape Colony</a></li></ul></section>
